{
  "description": "T537 - Aesculus hippocastanum (Horse Chestnut):\rReduce faulted limb / limbs by - Specified extent\treducing the scaffold limb/ stems attached at the union at 4 m, on the southern stem with significant HCBC damage (lesions, lifted bark, exudation), by around 4 m, to reduce loading on the weak union an minimise the potential for limb/stem failure. Final cuts should be made at suitable pruning points, leaving furnishing growth to minimise visual impact where possible. Additionally, lightly shape the adjacent remaining branches, exposed by the pruning work, directly surrounding the reduced scaffold limbs to provide a more natural shape, removing no more than 1 m from the exposed branches and pruning back to suitable furnishing growth.",
